<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$98 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$98 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian commercial paper market absorbed a total of A$98 million worth of promissory notes via tenders on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Building materials and energy group Boral Ltd lead the charge, selling A$40 million of its 90-day paper at five basis points over the corresponding bank bill mid rate.</p>
<p>The bank bill yield curve is little changed from Monday with physical flows having slowed to a trickle. &quot;It's the slowdown before Christmas,&quot; a Melbourne-based dealer said.</p>
<p>At 0045 GMT (11.45 a.m.) March bank bill futures were up one point to 93.75.</p>
